1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,083
You've met the Files tool.

2
00:00:01,083 --> 00:00:02,625
But there's a whole toolbox built in.

3
00:00:02,625 --> 00:00:06,000
Let's walk every group so you know what the agent can actually do out of the box.

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,219
Here's the whole set, grouped.

5
00:00:07,219 --> 00:00:08,681
Files and Terminal for your machine.

6
00:00:08,681 --> 00:00:10,022
Web and Browser for the internet.

7
00:00:10,022 --> 00:00:11,769
Media for generating images, speech, video.

8
00:00:11,769 --> 00:00:13,597
MCP for everything you connected last module.

9
00:00:13,597 --> 00:00:15,709
Skills, Agents, and Workflows for reusable behavior.

10
00:00:15,709 --> 00:00:16,603
UI for the side panel.

11
00:00:16,603 --> 00:00:17,862
And Swarm for multi-agent work.

12
00:00:17,862 --> 00:00:19,000
That's the built-in toolbox.

13
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:19,867
Let's try Terminal.

14
00:00:19,867 --> 00:00:22,649
Switch it on and run a real command in the working directory.

15
00:00:22,649 --> 00:00:26,481
But say this plainly on camera: the working directory limits files, not the network.

16
00:00:26,481 --> 00:00:30,130
A command runs with your user's permissions and can reach out over the internet.

17
00:00:30,130 --> 00:00:32,000
Terminal is powerful — treat it that way.

18
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,131
A quick one: the Web group.

19
00:00:33,131 --> 00:00:40,000
Switch it on and the agent can search the web and fetch pages — useful whenever a question needs something current that isn't in your files or the model's training.

20
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:40,607
A word on enabling.

21
00:00:40,607 --> 00:00:42,939
Tools are chosen per conversation — you decide which are on in each chat.

22
00:00:42,939 --> 00:00:47,602
A new chat starts with the built-ins enabled so it can act immediately, but the habit that matters is trimming: turn off what a task doesn't need.

23
00:00:47,602 --> 00:00:50,860
Because — and this is a theme for the rest of the course — forty enabled tools choose worse than five.

24
00:00:50,860 --> 00:00:53,000
When you want a fixed, reusable set, that's an agent, in Module 10.

25
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:56,481
The built-ins cover a lot — but the real power is that you can add your own.

26
00:00:56,481 --> 00:00:59,000
Next, we write a custom tool in JavaScript, end to end.

